@title Frontend Framework for Course Scheduling
@subtitle Options for the admin app rewrite
@author Internal Tools guild, Wrenfield University IT

The course-scheduling admin app has about 60 screens, five developers, and is mostly forms and tables. This page compares React, Vue and Svelte for the rewrite.

# Criteria

- Team familiarity
- Form and table libraries
- Hiring pool
- Bundle size
- Long-term support

# Comparison

table = Framework,Team familiarity,Form/table ecosystem,Bundle size (KB),Hiring pool; React,4 of 5 developers,excellent,142,large; Vue,1 of 5 developers,good,98,medium; Svelte,0 of 5 developers,fair,41,small

# Pros and cons

### React

- Pro: four of the five developers already know it.
- Pro: the data grid we need exists today.
- Con: the largest bundle of the three, at 142 KB.

### Vue

- Pro: smaller bundle, at 98 KB.
- Pro: a medium-sized hiring pool.
- Con: only one developer knows it.
- Con: a good form and table ecosystem, but not as deep as React's.

### Svelte

- Pro: the smallest bundle, at 41 KB.
- Con: no developers on the team know it.
- Con: a small hiring pool.
- Con: a fair form and table ecosystem.

# Recommendation

! React, mainly because four of the five developers already know it and the data grid we need exists today.

> "We are optimizing for the next five years of maintenance, not the first five weeks of building."
> — Hannah Osei, Guild lead

Svelte was the favorite in the prototype spike, and we will revisit it for smaller tools.
